{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:762c0c67667c302e","name":"Marsh Haunt","source":{"id":"source:reference-762c0c67667c302e","title":"Marsh Haunt","revision":25641,"timestamp":"2024-12-04T22:55:53Z","sha256":"967253eea74d62122e07223ef99eb46c377c816745df233ab790148c1d6d63c9","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25641","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Marsh%20Haunt&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-762c0c67667c302e","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Marsh Haunt is a dangerous, Force-using beast found far from civilization and is the source of many wild tales regarding \"Force Demons.\" The Marsh Haunt is a vaguely humanoid creature that inhabits fens, marshes, and other wetlands. Its green-grey skin is dull and peeling, which helps it blend into its marshy surroundings. The head of a Marsh Haunt is set deeply between its shoulders, with gleaming red eyes that, while not sentient, hold an instinctual cunning.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Marsh Haunts acquired their horrible reputation due to their ability to instill overwhelming fear in their victims, causing them to flee and making them easy prey. They prefer to attack using ambushes, but are fearsome and relentless once engaged. Like other creatures that naturally draw upon ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", the Marsh Haunt has learned its Force abilities by instinct, much in the same way that traditional predators learn to hunt.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Marsh Haunt Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Marsh Haunts are native to the world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Abraxin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Abraxin?action=edit&redlink=1"}," in the Tion Cluster, but can be found throughout ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mid Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mid_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"},". As befitting the name, Marsh Haunts are usually found in swampy areas. Marsh Haunts often work together in packs of two to eight creatures, with half of the creatures using ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mind Trick"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mind_Trick","referenceId":"reference:5c0f83fb6ec25f33"}]}," to terrify prey while the other half waits in ambush.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Marsh Haunt Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge Aquatic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 11 \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3 \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 23 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 23), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28, ",{"tag":"a